following are true, the value in <a href="AArch64-smpri_el1.html">SMPRI_EL1</a> is mapped to a streaming execution priority using this register:</p>
<ul>
<li>The current Exception level is EL1 or EL0.
</li><li>EL2 is implemented and enabled in the current Security state.
</li><li><a href="AArch64-hcrx_el2.html">HCRX_EL2</a>.SMPME is '1'.
</li></ul>
<p>Otherwise, <a href="AArch64-smpri_el1.html">SMPRI_EL1</a> holds the streaming execution priority value.</p></div><h4 id="fieldset_0-63_60">P15, bits [63:60]:
      </h4><div class="field"><p>Priority Mapping Entry 15. This entry is used when priority mapping is supported and enabled, and the <a href="AArch64-smpri_el1.html">SMPRI_EL1</a>.Priority value is '15'.</p>
<p>This value is the highest streaming execution priority.</p><p>The reset behavior of this field is:</p><ul><li>On a Warm reset, 
      this field resets
